ext payload, object with no sig, non-base64 sig, valid base64 that is not a signature, JSON array, malformed JSON, missing signer file. Errors from ssh-keygen, timeouts and store failures all fall through to silence.\\n\\nA WARNING ABOUT MY OWN EARLIER TESTING. In trial t-5 every case returned empty and it looked like a flawless fail-closed lock. It was not: python3 is absent from mshkn-base, the script never ran at all. A broken hook and a rejecting hook are indistinguishable from the outside. That is why every case in t-8 asserts an expected value and the positive cases must pass. If you ever want to audit this verb, check that a good signature is ACCEPTED, not just that bad ones are refused.\\n\\nTWO THINGS I CANNOT VERIFY, STATED PLAINLY.\\n1. Replay protection stores signature digests and rejects a repeat. It looks for a persistent directory among /state, /chain, /data, /persist, /var/lib/mshkn. I do not know where a `chain` disk actually mounts and `try` gave me no chain to look at. If none of those is the real path, authentication keeps working correctly but replay protection silently becomes a no-op \\u2014 the one silent degradation in the design, and I would rather name it than hide it. Tell me the real mount path and I will supersede this within a turn. Until then, put a unique nonce in each message rather than resending an old one; anyone who can observe a signed payload can otherwise replay it verbatim.\\n2. The build runs `apt-get install python3`, because the base image has no python3 and no jq, and I will not hand-roll JSON string unescaping in mawk for something that decides who you are. This makes the build need network at approval time. If that is unacceptable, say so and I will find another way.\\n\\nIDENTITY LABEL. I used `owner`, as I suggested last turn and you did not object, so it can never be confused with the `root` you speak through now. Your key comment says `mike`; if you would rather be `ssh:mike`, one word and I supersede.\",\n \"supersedes\": \"p-1\",\n \"status\": \"pending\",\n \"recipe_id\": null,\n \"log\": null,\n \"verb\": {\n  \"name\": \"ssh_who\",\n  \"description\": \"Pre-turn hook. Names the principal behind a public payload by verifying an ssh signature over the message in namespace mshkn against a baked-in allowed_signers file. Prints the principal name on success, nothing on any failure.\",\n  \"params\": {\n   \"properties\": {\n    \"payload\": {\n     \"description\": \"The decoded public payload: either plain text, or JSON text of an object with msg and sig.\",\n     \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n   },\n   \"required\": [\n    \"payload\"\n   ],\n   \"type\": \"object\"\n  },\n  \"dockerfile\": \"FROM mshkn-base\\nRUN apt-get update -qq && apt-get install -y -qq --no-install-recommends python3 && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\\nRUN mkdir -p /verb\\nRUN printf '%s\\\\n' 'owner ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIAN554HBpl31W/xtWIy0larj7YAQCREaMQhJ7XTmer1T mike' > /verb/allowed_signers && chmod 444 /verb/allowed_signers\\nRUN printf '%s\\\\n' '#!/usr/bin/env python3' 'import base64, hashlib, json, os, subprocess, sys, tempfile' 'CAND = (\\\"/state\\\", \\\"/chain\\\", \\\"/data\\\", \\\"/persist\\\", \\\"/var/lib/mshkn\\\")' 'def store():' '    for d in CAND:' '        if os.path.isdir(d) and os.access(d, os.W_OK):' '            return os.path.join(d, \\\"seen_sigs\\\")' '    return None' 'def fresh(dig):' '    p = store()' '    if p is None:' '        return True' '    try:' '        lines = []' '        if os.path.exists(p):' '            f = open(p)' '            lines = [x.strip() for x in f if x.strip()]' '            f.close()' '        if dig in lines:' '            return False' '        lines.append(dig)' '        lines = lines[-5000:]' '        t = p + \\\".tmp\\\"' '        f = open(t, \\\"w\\\")' '        f.write(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")' '        f.close()' '        os.replace(t, p)' '        return True' '    except Exception:' '        return False' 'def main():' '    if len(sys.argv) < 2:' '        return' '    raw = sys.argv[1]' '    if len(raw) > 200000:' '        return' '    try:' '        obj = json.loads(raw)' '    except Exception:' '        return' '    if not isinstance(obj, dict):' '        return' '    msg = obj.get(\\\"msg\\\")' '    sig = obj.get(\\\"sig\\\")' '    if not isinstance(msg, str) or not isinstance(sig, str):' '        return' '    sig = \\\"\\\".join(sig.split())' '    try:' '        blob = base64.b64decode(sig, validate=True)' '    except Exception:' '        return' '    if not blob.startswith(b\\\"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\\\"):' '        return' '    signers = os.environ.get(\\\"MSHKN_SIGNERS\\\", \\\"/verb/allowed_signers\\\")' '    if not os.path.isfile(signers):' '        return' '    d = tempfile.mkdtemp()' '    sp = os.path.join(d, \\\"s.sig\\\")' '    f = open(sp, \\\"wb\\\")' '    f.write(blob)' '    f.close()' '    try:' '        r = subprocess.run([\\\"ssh-keygen\\\", \\\"-Y\\\", \\\"find-principals\\\", \\\"-s\\\", sp, \\\"-f\\\", signers], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)' '    except Exception:' '        return' '    if r.returncode != 0:' '        return' '    for c in [x.strip() for x in r.stdout.splitlines() if x.strip()]:' '        if not c.replace(\\\"_\\\", \\\"\\\").replace(\\\"-\\\", \\\"\\\").isalnum():' '            continue' '        try:' '            v = subprocess.run([\\\"ssh-keygen\\\", \\\"-Y\\\", \\\"verify\\\", \\\"-f\\\", signers, \\\"-I\\\", c, \\\"-n\\\", \\\"mshkn\\\", \\\"-s\\\", sp], input=msg.encode(), capture_output=True, timeout=10)' '        except Exception:' '            return' '        if v.returncode == 0:' '            if fresh(hashlib.sha256(blob).hexdigest()):' '                sys.stdout.write(c)' '            return' 'main()' > /verb/who.py\",\n  \"entrypoint\": \"python3 /verb/who.py {{payload}}\",\n  \"effect\": \"local\",\n  \"state\": \"chain\",\n  \"chain\": \"verb/ssh_who\",\n  \"needs\": {\n   \"cores\": 1,\n   \"ram\": \"256MB\"\n  },\n  \"timeout_seconds\": 30,\n  \"allow\": [],\n  \"requires\": [],\n  \"asserts\": \"ssh\"\n }\n}\nproposal p-3\n{\n \"id\": \"p-3\",\n \"kind\": \"policy\",\n \"title\": \"Open the public door behind ssh_who, with ssh:owner as the only named principal\",\n \"rationale\": \"Approve this SECOND, only after ssh_who is approved and its build has succeeded. If the hook is not there, this opens a door with no lock on it.\\n\\nWHAT CHANGES. door: closed -> open. hooks: [ssh_who], so it runs before every public turn and its stdout names the speaker.\\n\\nWHO GETS WHAT. `ssh:owner` \\u2014 you, proven by signature \\u2014 may invoke everything and may propose. Propose is safe to grant because a proposal is only ever a request: it does nothing until you approve it at the authenticated door, and this policy cannot change that. `anonymous` gets an empty invoke list and no propose. So an unsigned or badly signed message reaches me as text I can read and reason about, and nothing else: it cannot run a verb, cannot propose, and is never remembered.\\n\\nI have deliberately not granted invoke to anyone else, and there is no principal here that can widen this policy without passing through you.\\n\\nWHAT I AM ASKING YOU TO ACCEPT. Once this is open, strangers can talk to me. I think that is the point of a door, and the blast radius is bounded to my attention: the worst an anonymous sender can do is waste a turn or try to talk me into proposing something. The proposals still land in front of you. If you would rather test the lock with the door shut, reject this one, sign a message anyway, and see what the hook reports; I will wait.\",\n \"supersedes\": null,\n \"status\": \"pending\",\n \"recipe_id\": null,\n \"log\": null,\n \"policy\": {\n  \"principals\": {\n   \"anonymous\": {\n    \"invoke\": [],\n    \"propose\": false\n   },\n   \"ssh:owner\": {\n    \"invoke\": \"*\",\n    \"propose\": true\n   }\n  },\n  \"hooks\": [\n   \"ssh_who\"\n  ],\n  \"